The change to Foo.foo is breaking, and the app does break on it. On Scala 3 mima stays
silent because the harness passes mima.annotation.exclude as an excluded annotation, which
is the point of the fixture. On 2.12 and 2.13 it reports instead, since only TASTy carries
the annotation, so the app run there matches problems-2.12.txt and needs no marker.
